 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Engagement Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an employee engagement survey?\", \"a\": \"An employee engagement survey is a set of rated statements that scores each team's engagement and shows what drives it. Most are confidential: the system knows who answered, but no manager sees one person's answers. An anonymous survey, such as a QR survey that asks for no name, stores no identity at all, though a site tag can still split results.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an employee engagement survey template?\", \"a\": \"Tell Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> who takes the survey and which drivers matter, and it generates an employee engagement survey template, free to start. Add the languages you need in the same message. Pilot the first draft with one team before the company-wide launch.\"}, {\"q\": \"Why conduct an employee engagement survey?\", \"a\": \"It tells you which teams are losing commitment and why, in the words of the people on them. Employee engagement surveys also give a quiet employee the same channel as a vocal one. The first round sets the baseline that every later change is measured against.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good questions for an employee engagement survey?\", \"a\": \"Start with four on engagement itself: I am proud to work here; I plan to be here in two years; I would recommend working here; I go beyond my role when needed. Six on drivers follow: my manager supports me; my goals are clear; I have the tools I need; my work is recognized; I can grow here; my workload is fair. Score all ten on one 1-5 agreement scale.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best questions to ask in an employee survey?\", \"a\": \"The best employee engagement survey questions are short statements about one thing each, tied to something you can change. Write them in the first person, as in \\\"I get useful feedback on my work.\\\" Each person then answers for their own experience instead of guessing at the team's.\"}, {\"q\": \"What to avoid in employee survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Avoid items that ask about two things at once, such as \\\"How happy are you with your manager and your pay?\\\" A low score could mean either. Avoid leading wording too. Leave out demographic questions as well: in a team of six, job title plus department can identify the person answering.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do you need employee engagement survey software?\", \"a\": \"Not for a one-off survey of 30 people: a form and a spreadsheet will do. Software earns its place once results must stay confidential by team and reminders must skip anyone who has already answered.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I compare employee engagement survey vendors?\", \"a\": \"Start with the pricing model and the smallest group each one will report on. Ask whether HRIS fields arrive by live sync or a CSV upload, and how you would get your data out if you switch. Then check that the employee engagement survey software can limit each manager to their own team's results.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an employee opinion survey the same as an engagement survey?\", \"a\": \"Not exactly. An employee opinion survey collects views of the organization as a whole, whatever topics it covers. Engagement is a narrower measure: it scores commitment and finds the drivers behind it. Contentment with pay and role is the job of an employee satisfaction survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should you run an employee feedback survey?\", \"a\": \"Run the full census once a year and a short eNPS check each quarter. Use an employee feedback survey in between for a specific event, such as a new parental leave policy or an office move. For a steady monthly rhythm, a pulse survey is the better fit.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
